Package: wlboard
Version: 0.3.0-1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Aleksander Kutycki <74899889+olekkut@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/olekkut/wlboard
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35)
Recommends: fonts-dejavu-core | fonts-noto-core
Description: Lightweight, customizable native Wayland virtual keyboard & panel editor
 wlboard is a native Wayland on-screen virtual keyboard written in Rust with
 dual-mode operation: floating desktop overlay (zwlr_layer_shell_v1) plus
 native Wayland input-method mode (zwp_input_method_v1 / zwp_input_panel_v1)
 for KDE Plasma Lockscreen and SDDM login screen support. Includes a built-in
 visual Panel Editor with 0.5-unit snap grid, Inverted-T half-height arrows,
 forward Delete, searchable 28-language catalog with Add/Delete management and
 automatic KDE layout registration, monochrome SVG symbol mode, 4 starter
 panels, live HSV theming, and saveable JSON User Presets.
